        "name": "CodieH",
        "username": "CodieH",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/codieh/{size}/1853_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-07-03T00:28:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So quick question about Prolo ladies and gents:</p><p>How do \"Defensive Sacrifice\" and \"Shared Burden\" interact with each other?&nbsp;</p><p>As both cards trigger when two or more damage is about to be applied to Prolo, my main confusion with this lies with the order of operation. So I guess two questions: 1.) Do they both trigger? 2.) If they do who chooses which one is applied first?</p><p>Also \"a Caterpillar of Silliness\" is my term for this because I just imagine Proletariat popping in and out of hexes in a slow circle around his attacker.</p><p>Thanks for the considerations, fellow heroes = )</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:59.110Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 6,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 30.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 13240,
        "topic_slug": "a-caterpillar-of-silliness-a-proletariat-question",
        "display_username": "CodieH",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
